nt\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CfRTc7abrRWQ2Typfg9oK\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_019gq5oTjrYMaTUEj1TDLP31\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"git log --author=\\\"attavo executor\\\" -5 --format='%H %an <%ae>%n%B---'\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":534,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":567211,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":534},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"ae622d81-efb9-4dda-92a0-5ebf75b0d73f\",\"uuid\":\"0a924c77-7c0c-4ddc-aec9-e9f0408c61c0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-26T04:58:41.550Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CfRTc7C2eN4Ks5tQ2RhcB\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_019gq5oTjrYMaTUEj1TDLP31\":{\"command\":\"cd /Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-219 && git log --author=\\\"attavo executor\\\" -5 --format='%H %an <%ae>%n%B---'\"}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_019gq5oTjrYMaTUEj1TDLP31\":{\"cwd\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-219\"}}}\n2147 {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_019gq5oTjrYMaTUEj1TDLP31\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"565520e5c5ac23696ee8cf10bb9861c7052084c2 attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\\nattavo: build #217, drive as a pass (reconciler R2)\\n\\nattavo drive N becomes one short pass: it fast-forwards its working\\ncopy to origin's branch (never while a worker holds it), reads the\\nitem's report, and acts at most once -- recovers a dead or hung\\ninvocation, or starts the next stage -- before returning within\\nseconds.\\n\\nStarting a stage is the lease: the pass writes the invocation marker\\nand pushes it as a plain fast-forward with no merge and no retry\\n(push_lease); a lost race or an outright refusal both undo the local\\nmarker commit and the pass starts nothing. On a pushed marker the pass\\nspawns `attavo worker N <build|verify> NN` in its own session, stdout\\nand stderr redirected to <git-dir>/attavo/<stage>-NN.worker.log; the\\nworker outlives the pass, runs the stage in-process, and touches\\n<git-dir>/attavo/<stage>-NN.heartbeat every ATTAVO_HEARTBEAT_S seconds\\nwhile it runs. The report and the pass read alive from the heartbeat\\nfirst, falling back to the invocation's pid only when there is no\\nheartbeat file; the stall bound decides hung, never died, so a dead\\ninvocation is recovered even with no [drive].stall_after_s declared.\\n\\nA review takes the forge checks the pass already read on the\\npre-marker head (ATTAVO_FORGE_CHECKS); attavo verify reads that file\\ninstead of polling when it is set. --again starts the next attempt of\\na stopped stage; --all runs one pass in every ../attavo-worktree-N\\nbeside the checkout; --until-ready repeats the pass in one process\\nuntil the level is the operator's or done, a check concludes red, or\\nthe checks have not concluded within ATTAVO_DRIVE_POLL_BOUND_S.\\n--recover is gone and exits 2 saying so.\\n\\nRetires the stage run and the forge poll inside the old synchronous\\n`attavo drive`, `--recover` as an operator's act, the refusal to\\nrecover without a stall bound, verify's own poll when a pass has read\\nthe checks, and the synchronous drive calls this repository's own\\ntests made.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n---\\n65ddae864df683d1f2727359039100b58a92d726 attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\\nattavo: fix the three open findings of #208 and #212 (item 214)\\n\\n- verify: a returned record (forge checks not green) now writes the\\n  real stub_ratio instead of a constant null; the diff-since-approval\\n  and spec_dir it needs are computed once, before the forge poll, and\\n  reused by both the returned and pass write sites.\\n- build: pop ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND from the executor's environment so\\n  an inherited export from whoever launched `attavo build` cannot\\n  restore the command #212 retired.\\n- select-tests: a deleted test file no longer selects itself into\\n  nothing; it falls through to the fail-safe whole-suite rule like any\\n  other path this selector does not know, per the operator's 2026-09-20\\n  ruling.\\n\\nThe builder's-own-typecheck finding is unchanged: #212's gate already\\nruns the type check on the final tree.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n---\\n22d65cf7f95ce91272d0453ea691699c03d69ef9 attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\\nbuild calibration for #212: a probe, one bounded test command, a gate without the suite, a selector that fails safe\\n\\n- [checks].probe (with the required probe_timeout_s) answers whether the machine can run the\\n  checks before the first build; a tenant without one is asked the old way; the feed says the\\n  question and the answer either way.\\n- attavo test N selects for every path the item changed since the default branch (committed or\\n  not, records aside), runs through [tests].run, exits as the run does, and at\\n  [tests].call_timeout_s ends the run and its process group and exits 124\n2151 {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CfRTceHJsYgk8URTawQUT\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01396tM6nGGvHjo6Vb7MC1tU\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"git add -A adapters/ attavo/ schema/ tests/ attavo.toml && git status --short\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":2431,\"